A bit of news from our side:

[*]we have received the approval from Steam to release the Playtest version – thus except for our own ambitions, nothing holds us from opening the access for the first set of players;

[*]we have switched to daily builds for this period, as we progress aggressively; in the last few days, we released versions 398, 399, 400, 400a, 400b and 401 (the last one is from yesterday);

[*]we have a few things missing, which we want to do, before we open the Playtest: translation into Japanese, Russian, and Simplified Chinese; edits for the tutorial (which is crucial to allow you to understand the system); updated tables of interaction of tokens (again, crucial to explain how the system works).

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/45451974/f7b13f942e35e703fae9eec11c0e61ee2d659f7e.jpg[/img]

Once we address these issues, we're ready to start with the Playtest.
